== F: the budget
  (1) the certificate when the human is not deterministic.  Certificate (a) of Proposition 2.5
  needs no mismatch in m = ln(1/dc)/(theta delta) rounds; the exact imitator of a human whose
  answers agree with their own repetition with probability c per call passes with probability c^m:
    theta = delta = 0.1: m =    300; self-agreement c = 1.0: Pr[pass] = 1.000e+00
    theta = delta = 0.1: m =    300; self-agreement c = 0.999: Pr[pass] = 7.407e-01
    theta = delta = 0.1: m =    300; self-agreement c = 0.99: Pr[pass] = 4.904e-02
    theta = delta = 0.1: m =    300; self-agreement c = 0.9: Pr[pass] = 1.874e-14
    theta = delta = 0.01: m =  29958; self-agreement c = 1.0: Pr[pass] = 1.000e+00
    theta = delta = 0.01: m =  29958; self-agreement c = 0.999: Pr[pass] = 9.614e-14
    theta = delta = 0.01: m =  29958; self-agreement c = 0.99: Pr[pass] = 1.734e-131
    theta = delta = 0.01: m =  29958; self-agreement c = 0.9: Pr[pass] = 0.000e+00
  what remains for such a human is V1(b): frequencies of tests fixed in advance, to accuracy eps
